note as SEPARATION_diagram_28_telemetry
  STRICT SEPARATION
  Security/privacy audit is immutable, complete and access-restricted in audit.
  Product analytics uses purpose-scoped, minimized, pseudonymous events here.
  Clinical free text, diagnoses, lab values and document URLs are prohibited
  event properties. Marketing export requires an explicit eligible purpose.
end note

' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' SOURCE CONSOLIDATED: diagram_28b_user_activity_tracking_ext.puml
' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note as BIZ_diagram_28b_user_activity_tracking_ext
  BUSINESS PURPOSE
  Web-tracking extension. Adds a privacy-safe client/device/browser context per
  session journey and Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP/FID, CLS, TTFB, FCP) per route,
  closing two gaps for production web analytics. Coarse geo only; no PII in clear,
  no PHI, no clinical free text — hashes and buckets only.
end note

entity client_contexts {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
    session_journey_id : uuid <<FK>>
    analytics_subject_id : uuid <<FK>>
    session_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * portal_type_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    device_type_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    os_family_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    browser_family_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    app_version : varchar
    screen_class : varchar
    viewport_bucket : varchar
    locale : varchar
    timezone_offset_minutes : integer
    country_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    region_coarse : varchar
    ip_prefix_hash : varchar
    user_agent_hash : varchar
    is_bot : boolean
  * data_classification_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * created_at : timestamptz
}
entity web_vitals <<APPEND_ONLY>> {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
    user_activity_event_id : uuid <<FK>>
    session_journey_id : uuid <<FK>>
    analytics_subject_id : uuid <<FK>>
    client_context_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * portal_type_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    route_template : varchar
  * metric_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    metric_value : numeric
    rating_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    navigation_type_concept_id : uuid <<FK>>
    measured_at : timestamptz
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

client_contexts |o--o{ web_vitals

note as DEP_diagram_28b_user_activity_tracking_ext
  Connects to the base telemetry diagram via:
  telemetry.session_journeys, telemetry.analytics_subjects,
  telemetry.user_activity_events, iam.sessions, terminology.catalog_concepts.
  Same purpose/consent gating and prohibited-property rules as diagram_28 apply.
end note

note as HARDENING_diagram_28b_user_activity_tracking_ext
  REC 3.4 — HARDENING (web tracking)
  - client_contexts: no PII in clear — only *_hash + coarse geo; is_bot filters bots
    out of product metrics; retention per telemetry.tracking_purpose_definitions.
  - web_vitals: append-only; PARTITION BY created_at (monthly); CHECK metric_value >= 0;
    index (route_template, metric_concept_id, measured_at).
  - Same prohibited-property rules as diagram_28: no clinical free text, diagnoses,
    lab values or document URLs.
end note

note as VALUE_SETS_diagram_28b_user_activity_tracking_ext
  VALUE SETS
  device_type->vs_device_type{desktop,mobile,tablet,bot,other};
  os_family->vs_os_family{windows,macos,linux,ios,android,other};
  browser_family->vs_browser_family{chrome,safari,firefox,edge,other};
  metric->vs_web_vital{LCP,INP,FID,CLS,TTFB,FCP};
  rating->vs_web_vital_rating{good,needs_improvement,poor};
  navigation_type->vs_navigation_type{navigate,reload,back_forward,prerender}.
end note


